  "discussion": "A small bump in the northwest swell will bring another peak of small surf to north and west-facing shores today that will fade tonight before a moderate north-northwest swell arrives Friday and continues through the weekend. Surf along north and west-facing shores should top out around seasonal average during the peak of the swell Friday afternoon and Saturday, then slowly decline late Saturday and Sunday as the dropping swell shifts more northerly and a smaller overlapping northwest swell arrives. Both swells will fade early next week. A new long-periond south swell builds today and may push surf along south-facing shores back above seasonal average through Friday. The swell will slowly decline Saturday through early next week. Surf along east-facing shores will begin to increase this afternoon into tonight as trade winds strengthen over the region. Rough trade wind swell will produce east shore surf above seasonal average Saturday through early next week.",
